{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.TwistSignTorsor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.TwistSignTorsor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Hom.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Defs"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.isUnit_unit_mul_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.isUnit_unit_mul_iff","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/TwistSignTorsor.lean#L102-L111","doc":"**Axiom 4 is sign-blind.** Scaling a datum by any unit leaves invertibility\nunchanged, so the Wedderburn conditions cannot separate the two ribbon\nstructures. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.no_constant_nonunit_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.no_constant_nonunit_sign","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/TwistSignTorsor.lean#L98-L100","doc":"A constant sign other than the identity is therefore **not** a twist sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.sign_trivial_on_squares","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.sign_trivial_on_squares","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/TwistSignTorsor.lean#L90-L96","doc":"**The flip is invisible on squares.** This is exactly why the braiding fixes\n`q = v²` while leaving `v` free, and it refutes the naive \"just negate `v`\neverywhere\": a constant sign `s ≠ 1` would need `ε (x * x) = s`, against\n`ε x * ε x = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.sign_trivial_on_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.sign_trivial_on_unit","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/TwistSignTorsor.lean#L87-L88","doc":"The flip never touches the unit object: `θ 𝟙 = id` survives it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.TwistSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.TwistSign","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/TwistSignTorsor.lean#L79-L85","doc":"A **twist sign**: the monoidal character by which two ribbon structures over\none braiding differ.\n\nModelling it as a *homomorphism* is the whole content. The ribbon axiom\n`θ (V ⊗ W) = (θ V ⊗ θ W) ∘ c ∘ c` forces `ε (V ⊗ W) = ε V * ε W`, so a sign\nassignment that is not multiplicative does not define a twist at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ExponentTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ExponentTwo","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/TwistSignTorsor.lean#L74-L77","doc":"**Exponent two** — the property that makes a sign group a `ℤ/2` grading\ngroup. Stated as a hypothesis rather than fixing `ℤˣ`, so the result covers any\ngrading group of exponent two. ","signatureChunk":0}]}